Original commit body from 319e8f26f3374950c4573212f7045a6fd5099e29:

ADR-0061 ruling 3 says a catalogue file's tier is its own provenance line,
never the directory. load_function_summaries ranked every
function_summaries.d file as the user's before reading that line, so a file
still declaring provenance: community was stamped user_supplied: its
terminating summary closed the taint branch (violated -> inconclusive, caveat
user_supplied_sanitizer naming "your own function_summaries.d/"), it won name
collisions over built-in rows, and --no-default-overlays kept it, while the
JSON tiers listed it as community.

The loader now asks the provenance line first: a community channel file
ranks with the shipped community files (adds only, stamped community, so the
walk withholds its terminating summaries and the violated verdict names them
as withheld_community_summary) and include_community=False drops it. In
verify-claims it is listed in tiers only when loaded, and under
--no-default-overlays it goes to omitted_community_overlays with family
function_summaries plus a stderr notice.

Same rule, io_primitives disclosure: a loaded community overlay named by
--io-primitives or a claims file's extra_catalogs was listed as USER-SUPPLIED
input with user_supplied: true. It now goes to named_community_files (family
io_primitives) beside the community taint files; its grants are still listed
as withheld, and the WITHHELD GRANTS text block now renders whether or not
anything was user-supplied.

Spec ADR-0061 status rows and docs/CATALOGUES.md updated.

